// expect: 134 trap: a precondition failed at tests/micros/mn-float-to-int-says:8:13 — the operand is outside the word
// `float_to_int` of a Float past what an Int holds traps in the
// instruction; where its claim stayed open at the argument, the checked
// conversion stops saying so at the call's address, where the engine's own
// trap said `integer overflow`.
fn big(n) = 1000000000000.0 * n

fn main() = float_to_int(big(2.0))
